geist (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add the native Win32 reader: one statically linked executable around the
    system WebBrowser control, per-monitor DPI aware with themed common
    controls, built with MSVC and MinGW-w64. It replaces the Qt reader in the
    Windows release; the macOS reader DMG is attached to the release as well.
  * Ship THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES with every binary distribution, and draw GDF
    vector text with the Hershey Roman simplex stroke font.
  * Type 99.7% of the topics of a fresh 500-book census with no word lost on
    the typed route: framed and captioned pictures, revision marks (including
    header-declared letter marks), CZ flow and list regions, footnotes,
    parameter and definition lists, generated indexes, contents and figure
    lists, drawn boxes and diagrams, glossaries and fixed-table selectors.
  * Model LNK cross-book links to figure, table and spot anchors through the
    resolve_cross_book hook, and keep pictures a book does not store as
    unresolved images in place.
  * Follow hosted BookServer for run-in CZ FLOW H headings, glossary terms,
    message anchors and generated-list labels, and document the new format
    findings in the BOO specification.

 -- Yvan Janssens <yvanj@cyber.gent>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:12:57 +0000

geist (0.3.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add the experimental universal native macOS reader, including multi-window
    file opening, drag and drop, book information and paginated printing.
  * Route every indexed topic and both HTML and Markdown renderers through the
    shared DocumentIR, with stable identities and independent conservation
    diagnostics.
  * Preserve compound lists, definitions and message catalogues, source-framed
    native artwork, revision controls, deferred fonts, anchors and thematic
    rules without opaque typed fallbacks.
  * Bind glyph and font coordinates to source UTF-8 spans and preserve complete
    ordered cross-reference claims, alternatives, styles and provenance through
    consumer resolver hooks.
  * Extend the corpus regression baseline to every indexed topic and document
    verified BOO message, native-row and control framing.

 -- Yvan Janssens <yvanj@cyber.gent>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:01:23 +0000

geist (0.3.3) unstable; urgency=high

  * Reject truncated GDF full-arc records and bound GDF raster work, cell
    arrays, coordinates, text and geometry from malformed BOO resources.
  * Limit encoded image bytes, decoded pixels and cumulative GIF frames before
    allocating or invoking the GIF, PNG and MMR decoders.
  * Evaluate object HEAD and conditional requests before image conversion;
    chunk Apache response writes and contain all C++ exceptions at the module
    boundary.
  * Preserve source-framed message introductions across record boundaries and
    validate prose headings against source evidence instead of TOC labels.
  * Pin Windows release recovery to the tagged source and the supported MSVC
    2022 toolchain; enable the conforming lambda processor for all MSVC builds.

 -- Yvan Janssens <yvanj@cyber.gent>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:15:42 +0000

geist (0.3.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix Windows caption handling and deploy Qt runtime dependencies before
    running tests, including binaries outside the reader's directory.
  * Add revision-aware HTTP validators and conditional responses to mod_geist;
    navigate the complete topic inventory in source order.
  * Preserve native topic titles, picture captions, source-ordered figures
    and source-attached inline glyphs across logical records.
  * Fix source framing, row ownership and generated-list labels; preserve
    native example rows, whitespace, font spans and links without inferring
    tables from aligned text.
  * Preserve publication emphasis and prevent indented publication numbers
    from creating false topic boundaries.
  * Verify emitted Markdown and HTML text independently and add an
    identity-pinned corpus regression gate with zero remaining word-loss
    allowances across 7,238 TOC topics in 33 private books.
  * Document reader-derived BOO variants, raw directory fields and observed
    malformed table text without rejecting unsupported variants outright.

 -- Yvan Janssens <yvanj@cyber.gent>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:25:40 +0000

geist (0.3.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Warm BooIndex shelves automatically without blocking Apache startup.
  * Persist shelf metadata across workers and restarts in GeistCacheDir;
    create the cache directory with worker ownership during installation.
  * Render Part-level chapter menus and documented vertical spacing forms.
  * Align the CMake and vcpkg release versions.

